# shared/api – Dependency Facades

All production runtime dependencies are wrapped as facades under `src/shared/api`.
Every access from app code goes through the barrel `@/shared/api`.

## Rules

- Add one facade module per dependency (e.g. `vue.ts`, `tauri.ts`)
- Re-export or wrap only what the app needs
- Put JSDoc on exported facade functions/variables
- Import facades only via `src/shared/api/index.ts`
- Never import `@tauri-apps/*`, `vue`, or other runtime deps directly from features/pages/widgets/entities/app

## Example

```ts
// shared/api/tauri.ts
/** Invokes the Tauri greet command. */
export async function greet(name: string): Promise<string> { /* … */ }

// shared/api/index.ts
export { createApp, ref } from "./vue";
export { greet } from "./tauri";

// feature
import { ref, greet } from "@/shared/api";
```
